<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="044" project="spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4">
  <metadata>
    <title>no-mock-identity test warm-up so a cold run does not time out (FR-29, #2275)</title>
    <phase>4 Access, sign-in, carry-overs, Teams</phase>
    <gate>after 038 (P3 deploy)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Test-only change (tags testing, unit-test); root CLAUDE.md §8 still requires code-review + adr-check because it modifies tests</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Scoped, mechanical change to one vitest file with a clear acceptance check</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>medium</effort>
    <parallel-group>E</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>038</deps>
    <tags>testing, unit-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1-2 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Warm the module graph of src/client/external-spa/tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx in a `beforeAll`, so the first run after an edit no longer hits the 60 s per-test timeout.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in vitest and Vite's module transform cache.</role>
  <goal>Two consecutive cold runs of the file after touching a source file it imports both pass, with no assertion changed or weakened.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>#2275: the file's tests dynamically import large modules (`../src/App`, `../src/pages/WorkspaceHomePage`, `../src/api/me-client`, `../src/auth/msal-auth`, `../src/auth/backend-selection`, `../src/auth/bff-client`) after `vi.resetModules()` in `load()` (:72-79), with `SLOW = { timeout: 60000 }` (:36). On a cold transform cache the first test that imports App pays the whole transform cost and times out. `vi.resetModules()` clears the module registry but not Vite's transform cache, so importing the same specifiers once in `beforeAll` (with its own generous hook timeout) moves the cost out of the tests.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/external-spa/tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/vitest.config.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/external-spa/tests/setup.ts</file>
      <file role="new-artifact">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-044-notes.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="038" status="pending">P3 deployed and E2E-proved (phase-deploy convention)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec FR-29">Change only the warm-up: no test is removed, skipped, renamed or has its assertions changed; the per-test SLOW timeout is not raised.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The warm-up imports only modules the file's tests already import, and must not leave state behind: tests still call `load()` (vi.resetModules) as today, and the warm-up runs before any env stub.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do not change vitest.config.ts or the global test timeout for the whole suite.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project wave E">This file is owned by this task in wave E; task 043 adds its 503 tests in a separate file.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>src/client/external-spa/README.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Fresh module graph per test" location="src/client/external-spa/tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx">`load()` (:72-79) — keep it; add the warm-up beside it.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Reproduce: touch a source file the test imports (e.g. src/App.tsx timestamp only), run `npx vitest run tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx` from src/client/external-spa, record the first-run timing and any timeout.</step>
    <step order="2">Add a `beforeAll` (with its own hook timeout) that imports the heavy specifiers once, then calls `vi.resetModules()` so tests start from a clean registry.</step>
    <step order="3">Verify: touch the source file again, run the file twice in a row cold; both pass. Record both timings in the notes.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the full external-spa test suite (`npm test`) and confirm it passes.</step>
    <step order="5">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="6">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-044-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a cold run still times out with the warm-up in place, STOP and report the measured timings rather than raising timeouts or splitting the file.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Run the external-spa vitest suite</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">src/client/external-spa/tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r4/notes/task-044-notes.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">After touching a source file the test imports, two consecutive cold runs of no-mock-identity.test.tsx pass; timings are recorded in the notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no test in the file is removed, skipped or weakened, and the per-test timeout is not raised.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">vitest.config.ts and the suite-wide timeout are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The full external-spa suite passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the warm-up only; no new test cases. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-29; issue #2275. Real path: src/client/external-spa/tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx (the spec's "tests/no-mock-identity.test.tsx" is relative to the SPA root).</notes>

